# DTF tier manifest: mcp-sync-interrupted-pass  (artifact-keeper#6390, 1.13.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + webhooks.mock-blackhole (hook-sink at
# 172.16.<slot>.79; its :81 accepts a request and never answers). The Remote
# MCP repository's upstream is that black hole, so a sync pass stays on its
# first page for as long as the oracle needs.
#
# THE BUG
# #6390  A Remote MCP sync pass that loses its process (pod loss, a panic, a
#        cancellation) releases the repository's sync lock when its database
#        connection drops, but records nothing. GET .../mcp/sync then answers
#        `running: false` with the previous pass's lastFinishedAt / lastError
#        (here none at all), so a client polling for the pass's end cannot
#        tell that it ended. Fixed: the first poll that finds the lock free and
#        a start with no later finish records the pass as ended, with
#        lastError "the sync pass ended without recording an outcome (...)".
#
# THE GATES
#   (CONTROL) every image: the manual trigger answers 202 and a poll sees the
#     pass running (lock held, lastStartedAt set, no lastFinishedAt) against
#     the black hole; after `docker kill` + `docker start` of the backend (the
#     loss of the pass's process) the backend is healthy again.
#   (FIX) #6390: the first poll after the restart answers running:false with
#     lastFinishedAt at or after lastStartedAt and lastError naming the pass
#     that ended without an outcome; a second poll answers the same record.
#     RED on main before the fix (lastFinishedAt and lastError null).
#
# The scheduled pass cannot interfere: the repository is not due (its pass
# started seconds ago; the interval is one hour) and the scheduler waits 90 s
# after startup.
#
# Wall clock: about 1 minute.
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: polls back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the black hole sits on a private address.
COVERS="6390"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem webhooks.mock-blackhole"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
